<description>
**Problem:** The mempool estimator added in #34075 checks health by comparing the weight of transactions removed from our mempool with the weight of recently mined transactions.
It gets the removed transactions from `removeForBlock` and counts their local weight.
That function matches mempool entries to block transactions by txid, which does not commit to witness data.
A matched entry can therefore have a different weight from the mined transaction, skewing the coverage check.
The block policy estimator also treats the local variant as confirmed even though its wtxid was not in the block.
Same-txid, different-witness transactions also appear in #35501 and #35893.

**Fix:** First, derive coverage from block transactions in one walk, using each transaction’s weight once.
The old sum of local weights hid the mismatch, so this change fixes the accounting directly and makes the calculation easier to review.
Then require an exact wtxid match in `removeForBlock` before reporting a mempool entry as mined.
A mismatched local variant is removed as a conflict, so neither estimator treats it as mined.
</description>

<commits>
847f90a0d7 test: characterize witness-weight coverage

A transaction ID does not commit to witness data. Record that the estimator counts a heavier local mempool variant and marks the window healthy even though the matching mined transactions fall below the coverage threshold.

7b785e3878 refactor: sum block weight with a loop

Use a coinbase-skipping loop to sum block weight. Continue summing
removed mempool entries separately so coverage values stay the same.

f0a30ff32c refactor: sum block coverage in one pass

Walk the connected block and matching mempool entries in one pass.
`removeForBlock` returns those entries in block order. Keep counting
the local variant's weight so the refactor preserves the existing
coverage result.

3a72a58a04 fees: count mined weight in coverage

Transactions with the same txid can have different witnesses in our
mempool and the connected block. Count each match using the mined
variant's weight so the local witness size cannot skew the health check.

f1de3523bf test: characterize same-txid witness removal

Record that removeForBlock reports a different witness variant as mined and does not send a conflict notification.

4cc6c2c1e9 mempool: classify witness mismatch as conflict

Only report a mempool transaction as mined when its wtxid matches the connected block. Report a same-txid witness variant as CONFLICT. The block policy estimator then removes the local variant from tracking instead of recording a confirmation. This may count as a failure for estimation targets the local variant already missed.

This also sends a removal event to wallet, ZMQ, and other validation subscribers. A wallet may issue an unconfirmed walletnotify before the block callback confirms the txid, and ZMQ sequence subscribers see a removal for a txid in the block.

08b3d87de8 doc: describe witness-mismatch block removals

Document exact-wtxid block removals, validation notifications, ZMQ sequence
behavior, and the block weight counted toward mempool coverage. Add release
notes for the observable notification and estimatesmartfee changes.
</commits>

